=== GS-UX-001 STEP 5 LANDS: 'A LABEL READING HOLD IS NOT A GESTURE' (ledger round 270) ===
utc: 2026-09-16T01:23:30Z
source_sha: e3642705f7e3c7a260f152c3d1b2e18b778022cf
argv (build): xcodebuild -project ios/Godstone.xcodeproj -scheme LabMesh -sdk iphonesimulator -configuration LightDebug CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build

THE CARD'S OWN SENTENCE, WHICH IS THE WHOLE STEP: "Implement SOS as an actual cancellable hold gesture with a monotonic
confirmation threshold and accessible alternative. A LABEL READING HOLD IS NOT A GESTURE."

WHAT LANDED, IN THE LAB'S OWN `LabSosView`:
  * A REAL HOLD -- `onLongPressGesture(minimumDuration: 0, pressing:perform:)` -- WHICH IS CANCELLABLE: releasing before
    the threshold reporteth 'hold cancelled -- threshold not reached', and only a hold that REACHED it armeth the SOS;
  * A MONOTONIC CONFIRMATION THRESHOLD, NAMED (`LabSosView.confirmationThreshold = .seconds(3)`) AND MEASURED WITH
    `ContinuousClock` -- NEVER `Date()` -- so a wall-clock step cannot arm it early. THIS IS THE SAME LAW THIS PROGRAMME
    ALREADY APPLIED TO THE GOVERNORS (rounds 187/195) AND TO THE CONNECTIONS' LEASE CLOCK (round 208);
  * AN ACCESSIBLE ALTERNATIVE: a `Button("Send SOS (accessible alternative)")` with its own accessibility label, BECAUSE A
    HOLD MUST NEVER BE THE ONLY ROAD -- a gesture that must be sustained is unreachable for some users;
  * and the screen SAYETH what it is doing at every stage (`hold to arm`, `ARMED -- release to send`, or the outcome).

THE BUILD, NOT A PARSE: **`BUILD SUCCEEDED` (rc=0)** on the simulator SDK, unsigned -- so the gesture COMPILES, unlike
round 262's file which 'parsed'.
AND THE INVARIANT: a SIXTH lab invariant asketh all three halves (a real gesture existeth; its threshold is monotonic; an
accessible alternative existeth), PROVEN TO JUDGE by a negative case in which the threshold was made to use `Date()` --
and the control FAILED with its named reason, restored rc 0.

AND ONE SLIP, RECORDED WITH THE REST: the invariant's FIRST wiring died on a HEREDOC ESCAPING ERROR
(`re.PatternError: missing ), unterminated subpattern`), the same family as round 251's `.format()` over code -- SO THIS
CONTROL WAS WRITTEN AS A FILE RATHER THAN A HEREDOC, and the mistake cost a call rather than a wrong invariant.
